<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mrs. Oakley returns one week after starting intramuscular cyanocobalamin for pernicious anemia. The practice nurse gave all seven daily injections. Her tongue is less sore and she has a little more energy, though she is still breathless on one flight of stairs. The tingling in both feet is unchanged, and she still feels unsteady in the dark. She has had no palpitations, muscle cramps, or leg swelling. She began physical therapy for her back five days ago and has done her home exercises daily. She saw Dr. Salib of hematology this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Tongue less sore; slightly more energy</td></tr><tr><td>Neurologic symptoms</td><td>Foot tingling and unsteadiness in the dark unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>Seven of seven daily injections given</td></tr><tr><td>Back pain</td><td>Physical therapy started five days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>No palpitations or cramps</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

